-> space_monologue

=== space_monologue ===

Space is a mysterious thing. #segment_break

A vast sea of stars that doesn't ever seem to end, filled with suns, planets, and things we've yet to even discover. #segment_break

No one knows just how dense our universe is, and humans will be long gone before they even know if there's someplace else where life blooms like it does on our earth. #new_page

#hide_window
#bg:asset/Visuals_Backgrounds/big_01_space_g0.png:crossfade:2000
#show_window

For now, all we can do is watch the stars lighting up our skies and attempt to uncover the wonders we've been blessed with, feeding our curiosity with theories, ideas and fantasies. #segment_break

A brightly lit sky is an inspiring sight, and why we've always had such a fanciful idea of the stars. #segment_break

But in the end, they're nothing but burning suns. #segment_break

Most have died thousands of years ago, yet we can still see the living corpse of what they used to be. #segment_break

It's even one of the closest things to time travel: #segment_break

Time shapes space, just as space shapes time. #new_page

#bg:asset/Visuals_Backgrounds/big_01_space_g1.png:crossfade:2000

For that reason, science will probably never attain the absolute truth of our universe. 

To think that all of those shiny things we see at night actually means the deaths of thousands of solar systems suddenly becomes a gruesome thought, instead of the sweet, dreamy fantasies we imagine. #new_page

And like people, stars shine bright before their death, as the remnants of our accomplishments scatter like light for everyone else to see.

And just like anyone else, I want people to see my life burning with passion and pride, before I become a corpse with nothing but my past to prove my existence. #new_page

#bg:asset/Visuals_Backgrounds/big_01_space_g2.png:crossfade:2000

After all, as a woman of science, I cannot believe in the afterlife. #segment_break

I need to prove myself, and make myself shine before I die. 

Like I said, ultimate truth will never be attainable: #segment_break

It's a holy grail, far from humanity's reach.

Many tried to play with their lives like they're some sort of god, but none of them lived long enough to come up with scientific facts. #new_page

-> euphie_introduction

=== euphie_introduction ===

#hide_window
#image:show:asset/Visuals_CG/cg01_spaceship.png:0:crossfade:1000:1280:720
#wait:1000
#bg:asset/Visuals_Backgrounds/bg00_shuttle.jpg
#show_window

And a researcher lives according to their facts.

This is why I'm standing here right now. #segment_break

Nervously talking to myself, trying to get rid of the anxiety slowly eating at me.

My name is Euphémia. #segment_break

But everyone calls me Euphie.

I'm 28, and I aced my astrophysics exams. #new_page

I went through intensive training to see if I was fit to navigate in space, and just as planned, passed without any issue.

I've been assigned to work as the head researcher and manager at the Orbital Station named SS-04, short for Stellar Sanctuary Number 04. #new_page

This is one of many stations like this placed in orbit around Earth. #segment_break

They're quite big and never require too much maintenance, so the staff is pretty limited in each station.

Don't know why they decided to pick someone as inexperienced and young as I to be the chief of some base I've never set foot on, but I guess that's thanks to my over-the-top results. #new_page

#audio:fadeoutbgm:2000
#cg:hide:1000

Suddenly, a synthetic voice jolts me out of my thoughts. #new_page

-> computer_announcement

=== computer_announcement ===

#layout:ADV
#audio:playse:asset/Sound/Sound_SFX/beep1.ogg

Arrival in five minutes. #segment_break

Please sit tight and make sure your belts are fastened as we approach Orbital Station SS-04. #speaker:Computer #color:#94b8b8 #new_page

#audio:playbgm:asset/Music/03_-_Space_Confessional_-_juneji.ogg
#layout:SNL

Sounds like we're nearly there. #segment_break

I've been to space before during my training, but it's the first time I'll be staying so long outside of the surface of the earth.

Kinda crazy to believe one can live so long outside of their own planet. #segment_break

I'll have to get used to it for the next few months. #new_page

Not like I'm really gonna miss Earth anyway. #segment_break

I'm excited enough just thinking about how great it must feel to learn more about what's surrounding our little blue planet.

It's hard to see as the ship is flying directly towards it, but I can make out the shape of the space station. #segment_break

It looks much bigger than I expected.

It's entirely white, with a giant tube as the supporting and main part of the station, surrounded by circular cylinders making up the many different floors. #new_page

-> ship_docking

=== ship_docking ===

#audio:playse:asset/Sound_SFX/engine_stop.ogg
#bg:asset/Visuals_Backgrounds/bg01_space_shuttle.png:crossfade:1000

The spaceship I'm on comes to a stop. #segment_break

The belts automatically unfasten themselves for some weird security reason, and I'm still the only one on the entire ship.

The two men in the cockpit sound like they're talking to someone over the radio. #new_page

I take a plastic bottle out of my bag. #segment_break

My throat feels dry.

Outside the little round window next to me, I could see the giant logo of the station's number on the perfectly white steel plates making up this strange structure. #new_page

-> pilot_dialogue

=== pilot_dialogue ===

#layout:ADV
#characterSprite:show:Pilot:neutral
#characterSprite:mod:Pilot:neutral_2

Are you ready to get onboard? #speaker:Pilot #color:#ffb366 #new_page

#characterSprite:mod:Pilot:neutral
#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:normal_shocked
Ah! #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#characterSprite:mod:Pilot:neutral
#layout:SNL

That guy surprised me. #segment_break

It's one of the pilots. #segment_break

I put my bottle back in my bag and get up. #new_page

I'd been sitting for so long, my legs felt weak. #new_page

#layout:ADV
#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:normal_speak

Y-Yes! #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#characterSprite:show:Pilot:neutral_2

Then please let us lead the way. #speaker:Pilot #color:#ffb366 #segment_break

Through this door, you'll find the station's Gravity Change Chamber. #segment_break

It'll acclimate your body to the station's gravity. #speaker:Pilot #color:#ffb366 #new_page

Once the process is done, you shall be greeted by Klaus, the senior past chief of the station. #speaker:Pilot #color:#ffb366 #new_page

#characterSprite:show:Pilot:neutral
#layout:SNL

I already know this kind of protocol by heart, but I can't act like a bratty know-it-all, especially since everyone else in this damn sector seems to be men double my age. #new_page

#characterSprite:hide:Pilot
#characterPortrait:hide

-> gravity_chamber

=== gravity_chamber ===

#bg:asset/Visuals_Backgrounds/bg02_corridor_A.png:crossfade:1000
#wait:1500

I enter the GCC (Gravity Change Chamber). #segment_break

Nothing too peculiar, I've done this countless times. #new_page

#audio:playse:asset/Sound/Sound_SFX/inside_spaceship.ogg:loop:3
#wait:1000

The air pressure starts to shift. #segment_break

It's really intimidating and weird the first time, but you end up actually enjoying how funky it feels. #segment_break

Or maybe I'm just weird. #new_page

#audio:fadeoutse:2000:3
#wait:2000

My body now feels much heavier than before, and the gravity feels like what you're used to on Earth. #new_page

#audio:playse:asset/Sound/Sound_SFX/door1.ogg:2
#wait:2000

The door to the station opens. #new_page

-> Klaus_meeting

=== Klaus_meeting ===
#characterSprite:show:Klaus:Klaus
#wait:1200

Right behind it, a tall and fierce looking man is standing there, crossing his arms. #segment_break

I'm taken aback a little, since his gaze is so intimidating it feels like he's about to scold me. #new_page

#layout:ADV
#characterSprite:show:Klaus:Klaus

I presume you are Euphémia? #speaker:Klaus #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:normal_neutral

C-Correct. #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:smile

Welcome to SS-04. #segment_break

You can call me Klaus. #segment_break

Unless you've forgotten something on the ship, if you would get onboard... #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:normal_speak

Oh, yes, of course. #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page


#bg:asset/Visuals_Backgrounds/bg02_corridor_B.png:crossfade:1000

-> corridor_tour

=== corridor_tour ===

#layout:ADV
#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:smile

I'll be your guide around the station until you feel like you've understood the layout of this place. #new_page

It might seem big and intimidating at first, but it's much easier to navigate than you might imagine. #segment_break

Even I have not been to half of the rooms here. #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page


#layout:SNL

His words are reassuring, and I start to wonder whether his fierce stance and expression was just a way of appearing more imposing and leader-like or not. #new_page

#layout:ADV
#characterPortrait:show:euphie:thinking_normal
Isn't that... #segment_break

Kind of important? #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Klaus:confused
What do you mean? #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:euphie:thinking_normal
Knowing about every single room the station has. #segment_break

If you run into any kind of problems... #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#layout:SNL

I asked bluntly, without realizing how condescending that might sound, especially seconds after coming onboard. #new_page

#layout:ADV
#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:closed
Eh, you've got a point here. #segment_break

#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:smile
But don't worry, I just said that I personally do not know about half of them. #new_page

We've got a certain someone who knows absolutely everything about them. #segment_break

Moreover, most are just spare or storage rooms, so nothing too important. #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:thinking_normal

How are there are so many unimportant rooms? #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:Klaus

This station used to be a spaceship. #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:normal_surprised

Now that's something I did not know. #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:thinking

I can't remember too well, but since it became obsolete for Earth-to-space transport, it was simply reassigned as a basic orbital station, and renamed accordingly. #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:normal_speak

I guess that's why it's so big. #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:Klaus

Correct. #segment_break

And also the reason why you don't have to worry about the general structure of the spaceship. #new_page

#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:thinking2

Usually, the unimportant rooms are only accessible to the engineers anyway, to avoid getting people lost in this titanic place. #new_page

#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:Klaus

But enough about that. #segment_break

For now, I'll be presenting you to the staff, and the most important places. #new_page

Let's start with the dormitory, so you can at least lay down your luggage. #segment_break

Those seem quite heavy. #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:normal_smile
Yeah... #segment_break

Thanks. #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#characterSprite:hide:Klaus
#characterPortrait:hide
#layout:SNL

I don't know why I brought so much. #segment_break

My own comfy pillow, clothes I probably won't be able to wear, books... #segment_break

I even brought some snacks I could never get up here. #segment_break

I have a sweet tooth, what can I tell you. #new_page

I follow Klaus inside the great corridor, suddenly realizing that my luggage really is heavy. #segment_break

Surely because of both the air pressure change and my fatigue. #new_page

#layout:ADV
#characterSprite:show:Klaus:confused

Aren't those too heavy? #segment_break

Do you want me to take one or two of those bags? #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:thinking_embarassed

N-No! #segment_break

I'm fine, don't worry about it. #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page
#layout:SNL

Truth be told, I should have accepted. #new_page

#layout:ADV
#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:closed

Good. Because there's around four more minutes of walking. #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:normal_shocked_teeth

Wh-! #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#layout:SNL

F-Four?! #segment_break

Now I just feel like an idiot. #new_page

#layout:ADV
#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:smile

I'm just kidding. #segment_break

The station is divided into multiple floors, and you access them through the central elevators just there. #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#layout:SNL

-> elevator_section

=== elevator_section ===

#bg:asset/Visuals_Backgrounds/bg03_elevators_front.png:crossfade:1000

Klaus came to a stop in front of the elevators. #new_page

#audio:playse:asset/Sound/Sound_SFX/beep1.ogg

#layout:ADV
#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:Klaus

For practical reasons, there are two different ones. #segment_break

They're just as easy to use as any kind of elevator. #segment_break

#audio:playse:asset/Sound/Sound_SFX/door1_soft.ogg

Now, if you would get inside so we can continue our tour. #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#bg:asset/Visuals_Backgrounds/bg04_elevators_inside.png:crossfade:1000

#audio:playse:asset/Sound/Sound_SFX/footsteps_light.ogg

Klaus goes in the elevator, and I follow him in. #new_page

#audio:playse:asset/Sound/Sound_SFX/door1_soft_2.ogg

The gate closes and the elevator starts to move slowly. #segment_break

#audio:playse:asset/Sound/Sound_SFX/elevator_up.ogg:loop

To break the silence, Klaus continues his explanations. #new_page

#layout:ADV
#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:closed

At the very bottom lie the escape pods. #segment_break

Obviously, we're only supposed to access them during emergencies. #segment_break

On floor -2 lie the server and engineering room. #new_page

Only the main engineer and technical staff have access to them: #segment_break

So Joshua, and Alexei. #segment_break

Floor -1 has nothing but spare storage rooms, accessible only to Joshua. #new_page

#characterSprite:mod:Klaus:normal

Basically, anything below the central floor is of no importance to you, so don't worry too much. #speaker:Klaus #color:#cc66ff #new_page

#characterPortrait:show:Euphie:normal_neutral

Easy enough. #speaker:Euphie #color:#ff8080 #new_page

#layout:SNL

#audio:fadeoutse:400:BGS/elevator_up.ogg
